  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Alligator** (1 review, 1 other source): Alligator and drums kept as one track because of the chants and guitar work leading into a jam; Reviewer singles out the Alligator into Caution sequence as essential listening, full of energy [1][2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Cryptical Reprise**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: drums [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1967-10-31.sbd.unclebarry-kikola.33933.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 6 songs; 45 min; rated 1.67/5 by 3 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1967-10-31.sbd.unclebarry-kikola.33933.flac16**: transferred by Uncle Barry and Tom Kikola; source: SBD?->unkown tape generation->HHB CDR830->NEC DVD_RW ND-3520A->EAC->CDWAV-FLAC [1]. Also: Source says this version is fake, assembled from material dated November 10th and 11th, 1967, not the October 31 show; Copy is exact, taken from a tape given by Uncle Barry; the only editing was done on Caution [1]",
